<!--
  COMPRINNO ARCHITECTURE SKELETON — 3-AZ THREE-TIER LAYOUT
  =========================================================
  Use this as the starting point for every new architecture diagram.

  HOW TO USE:
  1. Copy this file to outputs/<project-slug>/<project>.drawio.xml
  2. Replace PROJECT_NAME in both pages.
  3. Fill in the metadata (Date, Creator, Reviewer) in the title blocks.
  4. Add service icons into the labelled placeholder slots.
  5. Remove slots you don't need; add extra slots by duplicating an icon cell.
  6. Add the cluster lane(s) if compute spans AZ rows (see §14 in house-style.md).
  7. Add edges (all edges: parent="1").
  8. Fill in the Flow page.

  COORDINATE REFERENCE: .kiro/skills/arch-diagram/references/coords-cheatsheet.md
  FULL RULES:           .kiro/skills/arch-diagram/references/house-style.md

  GEOMETRY SUMMARY — container sizes follow the WRAP RULE (cheatsheet). Values below are for the
  shipped layout (single lane, public 1 icon):
    border:  x=0    y=-40 w=2570 h=2600  (w = cloud_x + cloud_w + 113)
    cloud:   x=260  y=250 w=2197 h=2115  (child of root; w = 247 + region_w + 85)
    region:  x=247  y=285 w=1865 h=1745  (child of cloud; w = 85 + vpc_w + 85)
    vpc:     x=85   y=260 w=1695 h=1405  (child of region; w = 520 + az_w + 65)
    az1:     x=520  y=80   w=1110 h=340   (child of vpc; w = content_right + 40)
    az2:     x=520  y=540  w=1110 h=340
    az3:     x=520  y=1000 w=1110 h=340
    icons in subnets: w=120 h=120, y=65, x=centred
    igw: x=-60 y=650 (child of vpc)      alb: x=160 y=650 (child of vpc)
  If the subnet columns change (2-icon subnet, dual lanes, ...) recompute the five container widths with the
  wrap rule and RE-CENTRE the regional row and global band (validate-drawio.py enforces both).

  SUBNET COLUMNS (relative to AZ): public x=35 | 40 | app | 40 | db   (x = previous right edge + 40)
    Width by icon count: 1 icon w=300, 2 icons w=380, 3 icons w=520.
    Lane exception: app_w = lane_w + 55 (35px left / 20px right gap).
    SHIPPED (lane-ready): public x=35 w=300 | app x=375 w=355 | db x=770 w=300  -> content_right=1070.
    No lane and 1 direct app icon: app w=300 -> db x=715 -> re-run the wrap rule.

  LANE GEOMETRY (relative to vpc, only add when compute spans AZs):
    lane_x = az_x + app_x + 35 = 520 + 375 + 35 = 930      (35px left / 20px right gap)
    Single lane:  x=930 y=170 w=300 h=1110   (dual: w=240 each, x=930 and 1190, app_w=555)
    Task icons:   x=90  y=25 / 485 / 945     (AZ-1/2/3, children of the lane)
    Badge:        x=938 y=178 w=45 h=45      (child of vpc)
-->
<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net" pages="2">

